
==Topi==

===[[Image:Open book 01.svg|30px|link=help:karazan-teny]] Anarana iombonana [[sokajy:topi]][[Catégorie:Anarana iombonana amin'ny teny topi]]===
'''aîaîá''' 
# ny spoonbill [[mavokely]] (Platalea [[ajaja]] (karazana))
#* ''Ha outra ave, a que os indios chamam '''ayayá''', que é do tamanho de uma franga toda vermelha, tem o bico verde, os pés pretos e o cabo do bico amaçado como pata; fazem seus ninhos em arvores altas, e mantem-se da fruta d’ellas. – 216, tpw, 1, There's another bird, that the Indians call “aîaîá”. It's the size of a chicken and all red, has a green beak, black feet and the beaks's shaft is squeezed like of a duck; they nest on tall trees and feed on their fruit.''
#* ''Braſilienſibus, Colherado Luſitanis, Belgis Lepelaer: Avis figura conveniens cum Europæis, ſolo colore differens. Anſeris magnitudine. Roſtro inſtar cochlearis lato, albo: collo longo, pedibus latis. Tota alba eſt, ſed in dorſo & alis dilute incarnati coloris perſplendentis. Caro illius edulis, & ſæpe comedi. Frequens eſt ad Flumen S Franciſci, & alibi paſſim in locis paluſtribus. – VIII, 204, tpw, 1, [It is called] aîaîá by the Brazilians, Colherado by the Portuguese, and Lepelaer by the Belgians: The bird's figure is accordant with the European (birds), differing only in colour. The size of a goose. As for the beak, equal in form to a spoon, it is white and wide: [it has] a long neck with wide feet. It is all red, but on the back and wings a bright diluted flesh colour. Its flesh is edible, and I have often eaten it. It is often at the São Francisco River, and elswhere it is here and there in swampy places.''

